  "bibliographyPath": "references.bib",
  "body": {
    "sections": [
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "content": [
              {
                "text": "In recent years, infrared small-target detection (IRSTD) has gained increasing impor tance in diverse applications such as ecological and environmental monitoring ",
                "type": "text"
              },
              {
                "keys": [
                  "2006Random"
                ],
                "mode": "parenthetical",
                "type": "citation"
              },
              {
                "text": ", maritime search and rescue ",
                "type": "text"
              },
              {
                "keys": [
                  "10703135"
                ],
                "mode": "parenthetical",
                "type": "citation"
              },
              {
                "keys": [
                  "10695116"
                ],
                "mode": "parenthetical",
                "type": "citation"
              },
              {
                "text": ", and military reconnaissance ",
                "type": "text"
              },
              {
                "keys": [
                  "10508299"
                ],
                "mode": "parenthetical",
                "type": "citation"
              },
              {
                "keys": [
                  "Philipp2011Efficient"
                ],
                "mode": "parenthetical",
                "type": "citation"
              },
              {
                "text": ". This is primarily attributed to the superior properties of infrared radiation, its longer effective range and stronger pene tration capability compared to visible light. In IRSTD tasks, typical targets include drones, aerostats, and ships, which generally exhibit the following characteristics ",
                "type": "text"
              },
              {
                "keys": [
                  "wang2019miss"
                ],
                "mode": "parenthetical",
                "type": "citation"
              },
              {
                "text": ": (i) Lowtar get energy. Duetosevere signal attenuation over long-range propagation, the received infrared signal is very weak, resulting in extremely low contrast between the target and the strong background clutter. Consequently, the target is easily overwhelmed by background noise. (ii) Small target size. Under long-range imaging conditions, targets often span only a handful of pixels, lacking discernible texture, shape, or structural information. (iii) Complex background. Real-world scenarios frequently involve numerous interfering elements, such as edges, corners, and other salient structures that significantly hinder the accurate separation of small targets from the background.",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "n3",
            "type": "paragraph"
          },
          {
            "content": [
              {
                "text": "To address these challenges, numerous IRSTD methods have been proposed. Existing approaches fall broadly into two categories ",
                "type": "text"
              },
              {
                "keys": [
                  "shen2023survey"
                ],
                "mode": "parenthetical",
                "type": "citation"
              },
              {
                "text": ": model-driven methods and data-driven methods. Model-driven methods ",
                "type": "text"
              },
              {
                "keys": [
                  "ahn2019weakly",
                  "bearman2016s",
                  "chen2013local",
                  "chen2023designing",
                  "cui2025weakly",
                  "dai2015boxsup",
                  "dai2017reweighted"
                ],
                "mode": "parenthetical",
                "type": "citation"
              },
              {
                "text": " explicitly incorporate prior knowledge specific to the IRSTD task, offering high interpretability. However, they exhibit limited robustness in diverse real-world scenarios and often require manual parameter tuning to achieve satisfactory performance. In recent years ",
                "type": "text"
              },
              {
                "keys": [
                  "shen2023survey",
                  "dai2021asymmetric",
                  "dai2021attentional",
                  "deshpande1999max",
                  "gao2013infrared",
                  "han2014robust",
                  "han2019local",
                  "HE2025131688",
                  "wsss2024review",
                  "kou2023detection"
                ],
                "mode": "parenthetical",
                "type": "citation"
              },
              {
                "text": ", data-driven methods , particularly deep learning approaches, have attracted widespread attention because of their superior performance and robustness. Nevertheless, most of these methods depend on pixel-level annotations for network training, underscoring the demand for large-scale, high-quality mask labels ",
                "type": "text"
              },
              {
                "keys": [
                  "kou2023detection",
                  "kou2024mcgc",
                  "li2022dense"
                ],
                "mode": "parenthetical",
                "type": "citation"
              },
              {
                "text": ". In practice, however, acquiring pixel-level annotations for infrared small targets is extremely costly in terms of human labor and time ",
                "type": "text"
              },
              {
                "keys": [
                  "li2023monte"
                ],
                "mode": "parenthetical",
                "type": "citation"
              },
              {
                "text": ". Moreover, the tiny scale and poor visibility of infrared small targets render manual pixel-level labeling highly subjective and error-prone, often yielding low-quality annotations.",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "n21",
            "type": "paragraph"
          },
          {
            "id": "n24",
            "label": "",
            "latex": "a^b_c",
            "numbered": true,
            "type": "equation"
          },
          {
            "alt": "",
            "assetId": "a1",
            "caption": [
              {
                "text": "IRSTD target",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "n15",
            "label": "",
            "span": "single",
            "type": "figure",
            "width": "75"
          },
          {
            "alt": "",
            "assetId": "a11",
